  recipeId: diagnostics
  concept: 'Authored objective: Repair all three faults and retest.

    Authored
    requirement: Diagnose the open V05, incorrect R2 value and Q1 bridge. Isolate
    power for each repair and verify a fresh run.

    General teaching principle:
    Troubleshooting compares fresh evidence with a known reference, isolates likely
    causes, repairs the supported issue and retests.

    Only fresh, authoritative
    game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: Debugging a chain is easier when each link is tested before replacing
    the next.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: An absent output is a symptom, not definitive proof that one specific
    component has failed.
